<h3>2. Ninja Fit Portable — Best Power</h3>
<p>Ninja brings its renowned motor expertise to the portable space. The 700-watt brushless motor is the most powerful in this lineup, crushing ice and tough frozen ingredients with ease. The 24-ounce capacity is the largest on this list, making it ideal for substantial breakfast smoothies.</p>
<p>USB-C charging means you can power it from any modern charger, and the one-touch operation with pulse feature gives you precise control over texture. It's slightly heavier at 1.6 pounds but the performance more than compensates.</p>

<h3>3. NutriBullet Go — Best Brand Trust</h3>
<p>NutriBullet is a household name in blending, and the Go carries that reputation forward. The extractor blade design efficiently breaks down cell walls in fruits and vegetables, extracting maximum nutrition. The 18-ounce cup is generously sized, and the compact charging base fits neatly on any countertop.</p>
<p>One standout feature is the integrated carrying strap — genuinely useful for taking this blender to the park, beach, or office. Battery life is solid at 15-18 blends per charge.</p>

<h2 id="sec-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>How long does a portable blender battery last?</h3>
<p>Most quality portable blenders deliver 15-20 blends per charge, with USB-C models trending toward the higher end. A full charge typically takes 2-3 hours. We recommend choosing a model with at least a 400mAh battery for reliable daily use.</p>

<h3>Can portable blenders crush ice?</h3>
<p>Yes, but with caveats. Models with 300+ watts and 4+ blades handle small ice cubes well. For crushed-ice textures, add 4-6 cubes and pulse briefly. The Ninja Fit Portable and BlenderBottle Blender Pro excel here.</p>

<h3>Are portable blenders easy to clean?</h3>
<p>Most modern portable blenders feature a self-clean mode: add warm water and a drop of dish soap, then blend for 20-30 seconds. Rinse thoroughly. The BlenderBottle Blender Pro and Omega Power Pocket have the most effective self-cleaning systems.</p>

<h3>What size portable blender should I get?</h3>
<p>For single servings, 14-16 ounces is ideal. If you prefer larger smoothies or meal-replacement shakes, opt for 18-24 ounces. All models in our list fall within practical carrying dimensions.</p>

